{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-37767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/assets/8de0dad0436135ef40aa26666d10659f4041275a915de153b6b4b45312c1c52f.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∬}_{D}{x}^{2}y\\,dA,$ where $D$ is the region shown in the picture above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-37767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The region $D$ can be partitioned into three type II regions ${D}_{1},$ ${D}_{2},$ and ${D}_{3},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/assets/b58fc3909d5be467999053336f67d41b88b43c984208c60f3d46ee8b7479df58.png)\n\nAs a result, we get \n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,-2\\le x\\le -1},\n$$\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,1\\le x\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{3}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-2\\le x\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{x}^{2}y\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}{x}^{2}y\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}{x}^{2}y\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{3}}{x}^{2}y\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{y\\text{ }\\,{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{-2}^{-1}\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{y\\text{ }\\,{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{y\\text{ }\\,{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7y}{3}\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7y}{3}\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{16y}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{7}{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{16}{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}+\\frac{64}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{71}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-37767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d8bcbb83491d7e12c6d27996e22f4fbab3af4ba87446264e370e4832bc95200"} {"question" "q-37767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-37767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{81}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{41}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{51}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{61}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{71}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-37767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{71}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-82135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/assets/4174f3930bb19223300539e1b4e9b7b191669aa4f701bff51e8349d0710ce6fb.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curves $y={e}^{x},$ $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ and the lines $y=1+e-x$  and $y=1-x,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-82135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={e}^{x} & \\,⟹\\,x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\ y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,x={e}^{y} \\\\ y=1+e-x & \\,⟹\\,x=1+e-y \\\\ y=1-x & \\,⟹\\,x=1-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/assets/4df7cf2f33520a80270341d4a40b4a83d9f3c11ed8adb69fe1131a42bcd61d5a.png)\n\n    \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,1-y\\le x\\le {e}^{y}}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le e,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\le x\\le 1+e-y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{{e}^{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1+e-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-82135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d8bcbb83491d7e12c6d27996e22f4fbab3af4ba87446264e370e4832bc95200"} {"question" "q-82135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-82135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{\\int }_{1-y+e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1/2}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{{e}^{2}y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2e}{\\int }_{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1+e-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1+e-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{{e}^{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1+e-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1-y}^{{e}^{y}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy+{\\int }_{2}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{e-y}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-82135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{{e}^{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1+e-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-82358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=\\sqrt{x-2}+1,$ and the lines $y=2-\\frac{1}{2}x$ and $y=8-2x.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-82358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=\\sqrt{x-2}+1 & \\,⟹\\,x=(y-1)^{2}+2 \\\\ y=2-\\frac{1}{2}x & \\,⟹\\,x=4-2y \\\\ y=8-2x & \\,⟹\\,x=4-\\frac{1}{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/assets/3f8e3ccfeac236d7fe9a502f599c61c404607a55ae809ec142019a3f881e1568.png)\n\n  \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/assets/3148cb0f499564db9cbfd6b635fef81dc47298789241af4a243c32dbf4dc8247.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,4-2y\\le x\\le 4-\\frac{1}{2}y}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,(y-1)^{2}+2\\le x\\le 4-\\frac{1}{2}y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{4-2y}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-82358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d8bcbb83491d7e12c6d27996e22f4fbab3af4ba87446264e370e4832bc95200"} {"question" "q-82358" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-82358" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{4-2y}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-2y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{4-2y}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{4-2y}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{4-2y}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-82358" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{4-2y}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-132287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/assets/d185077fab32b6f2c85e53550da2f04f1128eb14610764ad131ed50d8bbc6ff0.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the line $y=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2,$ and the lines $y=-x$ and $y=x,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-132287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/assets/47eccc29cbbdd917a247dec2f10329f718ed133b7e8398312b4ee3bc6bbbd647.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,-x\\le y\\le \\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,x\\le y\\le \\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-132287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d8bcbb83491d7e12c6d27996e22f4fbab3af4ba87446264e370e4832bc95200"} {"question" "q-132287" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-132287" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-x}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-132287" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-132490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/assets/71f160891f01681b485b2eb88dccf63b05271fab8e24f069e3bab46f4168c454.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∬}_{D}6x\\,dA,$ where $D$ is the region shown in the picture above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-132490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/assets/bb95d1507eb1cd527b6d6983cc0531d71c3852db002f188f220954a367de8d95.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,-\\sqrt{y+2}\\le x\\le -\\sqrt{2-y}}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y+2}\\le x\\le 0}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}6x\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}6x\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}6x\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+2}}^{-\\sqrt{2-y}}6x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+2}}^{0}6x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{-\\sqrt{y+2}}^{-\\sqrt{2-y}}\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{3}3{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{-\\sqrt{y+2}}^{0}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3[{(-\\sqrt{2-y})}^{2}-{(-\\sqrt{y+2})}^{2}]\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{3}3[{0}^{2}-{(-\\sqrt{y+2})}^{2}]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3(-2y)\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{3}3(-y-2)\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-3{\\int }_{0}^{2}2y\\,\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{2}^{3}(y+2)\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-3{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-3(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+2y){|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =-3(2)^{2}-3(\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2}+2(3))+3(\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}+2(2)) \\\\  & =-12-\\frac{63}{2}+18 \\\\  & =-\\frac{51}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/state.json" "file_sha256" "933b9d334d9511ede69480f9f61f7523f9f083e377ededa2f961ed170201b484"} {"question" "q-132490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082081/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d8bcbb83491d7e1